[size=4][b]How It Works[/b][/size]

If you are new to this kind of mod, the idea is very simple:

[list]
[*]The [b]Mod Loader[/b] lets StarRupture load plugin mods[/*]
[*]This plugin runs while your game is open and reads the state of your current session[/*]
[*]Press [b]F8[/b] and the map opens as a panel over the game[/*]
[*]In dedicated-server play, the client and server builds of [b]MapExtension_Plugin[/b] exchange map and rupture data with each other[/*]
[/list]

The mod only [b]observes[/b]. It does not automate anything, does not change your save and does not send commands to the game.

[line]

[size=4][b]What You Will See[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Where your cargo buildings are, which ones are connected, and which items travel through those links[/*]
[*]Where teleporters, players and your base cores are[/*]
[*]The state and charge of every monolith, and which base an attack is heading for[/*]
[*]Which antennas are activated[/*]
[*]Which abandoned bases you have discovered and what is left in them[/*]
[*]Where extractor deposits are, and how pure they are[/*]
[*]The current rupture phase and its resource[/*]
[/list]

The built-in world catalog shows deposits, plants and points of interest right away, with no scan or exploration needed. These positions are pre-generated; they are not live observations.

[line]

[size=4][b]Solo And Dedicated Server Support[/b][/size]

The plugin works in both solo and multiplayer.

[list]
[*][b]Solo / local-host:[/b] the plugin reads everything locally from the running game[/*]
[*][b]Dedicated server:[/b] install the server build of [b]MapExtension_Plugin[/b] on the server so the client and server plugins can exchange map, POI, and rupture data[/*]
[/list]

[b]Important:[/b] dedicated-server synchronization uses protocol v6 and requires matching protocol versions. Update the client and dedicated-server builds together; a mixed-version pair ignores incompatible packets and cannot synchronize a remote snapshot.

