[size=4][b]Quick FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Does this replace the in-game map?[/b]

No. It is an extra map panel, opened with F8, focused on logistics and world state.

[b]What happened to MapExtensionViewer.html?[/b]

It was removed in 0.8. The map is now inside the game. You can delete the HTML file and the [b]map-tiles[/b] and [b]map-data[/b] folders you kept next to it.

[b]The map opens but deposits and plants are missing.[/b]

The [b]MapExtension[/b] folder is not next to the DLL. Copy it again from the client archive into [b]ModLoader\Plugins[/b].

[b]Nothing happens when I press F8.[/b]

Check that [code][InGameMap] Enabled=1[/code] in [b]MapExtension_Plugin.ini[/b]. A config file created by an older version may still say 0.

[b]Monoliths show no state after a game update.[/b]

Their state is read for a specific game build. After a game update the Mod Loader switches off that single feature until the mod is updated. Everything else keeps working.

[b]Is this a client-side mod?[/b]

Yes. [b]MapExtension_Plugin[/b] is installed on the client.

[b]Do I need anything on a dedicated server?[/b]

Yes. For dedicated-server play, install the server build of [b]MapExtension_Plugin[/b] in the server [b]ModLoader\Plugins[/b] folder so the client and server plugins can exchange data.

[b]Does the mod update itself?[/b]

Yes, as long as you installed from the client archive so that [b]MapExtension_Plugin.json[/b] sits next to the DLL in your [b]ModLoader\Plugins[/b] folder. Only the plugin DLL is updated automatically.

